Executor Framework + Virtual Threads Cheat Sheet
1. Why ExecutorService?
Interview Question

Why not create threads manually?

❌ Bad

for(int i=0;i<1000;i++) {
    new Thread(task).start();
}


✅ Good

ExecutorService executor =
        Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);

executor.submit(task);

Simple Answer
Creating threads is expensive.

ExecutorService reuses threads.

One-Liner
ExecutorService = Thread Pool Manager.

2. Runnable vs Callable
Runnable
Runnable task =
        () -> System.out.println("Hello");


Returns:

Nothing

Callable
Callable<String> task =
        () -> "SUCCESS";


Returns:

Value

One-Liner
Runnable = No Return
Callable = Return Value

3. Future
Scenario

Need result later.

Future<String> future =
        executor.submit(task);

String result =
        future.get();

Problem
future.get();


blocks current thread.

One-Liner
Future is blocking.

4. CompletableFuture
Scenario

Call API asynchronously.

CompletableFuture<String> future =
      CompletableFuture
      .supplyAsync(() -> "Hello");

One-Liner
CompletableFuture is non-blocking.

5. Multiple APIs
Scenario

Need Customer + Account + Fraud APIs.

CompletableFuture<String> customer =
        getCustomer();

CompletableFuture<String> account =
        getAccount();

CompletableFuture<String> fraud =
        getFraud();

CompletableFuture
        .allOf(customer,
               account,
               fraud)
        .join();

One-Liner
allOf() waits for all tasks.

6. thenApply vs thenCompose
thenApply

Input

User


Output

String

future.thenApply(
      user -> user.getName());

thenCompose

Input

User


Output

CompletableFuture<Account>

future.thenCompose(
      user ->
      getAccount(user));

One-Liner
thenApply = Value to Value

thenCompose = Future to Future

7. Fixed Thread Pool
Scenario

Payment API handling requests.

ExecutorService executor =
     Executors.newFixedThreadPool(20);

One-Liner
FixedThreadPool limits concurrent threads.

8. Scheduled Executor
Scenario

Run every 5 seconds.

ScheduledExecutorService executor =
      Executors
      .newScheduledThreadPool(1);

executor.scheduleAtFixedRate(
      task,
      0,
      5,
      TimeUnit.SECONDS);

One-Liner
ScheduledExecutor = Cron Job inside Java.

9. Virtual Thread
Scenario

Need 100000 concurrent requests.

Thread.startVirtualThread(
        () -> process());

One-Liner
Virtual Threads are lightweight JVM threads.

10. Virtual Thread Executor
Recommended Java 21
try(var executor =
      Executors
      .newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {

      executor.submit(
              () -> process());
}

One-Liner
One Virtual Thread per task.

